  "reasoning": "The patient presents with sudden peeling of skin on the arms, legs, and back, along with joint pain and spreading skin rashes. This specific combination of widespread peeling/scaly skin lesions and joint pain is highly characteristic of psoriasis, an autoimmune condition that frequently manifests as inflamed, scaly plaques and can progress to psoriatic arthritis. While other conditions like fungal infections or viral rashes may cause skin changes, they do not typically present with prominent joint pain and widespread peeling skin simultaneously. Based on the symptom profile matching known clinical patterns, psoriasis is the most accurate diagnosis.",
